    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest score of 73.46 thanks to a leadoff role against the middling Rhett Lowder. **Jonathan Aranda** (70.46) and **Bryce Harper** (69.08) also project as elite anchors; **Aranda** benefits from a massive park-factor boost and a favorable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano, while **Harper** maintains high efficiency despite Jake Irvin\u2019s presence on the mound. **Daulton Varsho** (67.93) and **JJ Bleday** (66.16) remain high-value starts, with **Bleday** particularly well-positioned to exploit his platoon advantage against Jacob Lopez. Meanwhile, **Tyler Freeman** (69.91) serves as a critical engine for our stolen base targets; while he faces a tough assignment against Nick Martinez, his underlying projection is buoyed by park factors and a strong middle-order expectation.\n\nThe most difficult exclusion today was **Kyle Karros**, who posted a respectable 61.40 but ultimately yielded his spot to the higher-floor veterans in our utility and MI slots. While **Karros** enjoys favorable park and matchup conditions, the optimizer prioritized the consistent daily efficiency of **Luis Arraez** (60.13) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (62.15). We are keeping a close eye on **Cal Raleigh**, whose score has dipped to 41.82 due to a suboptimal matchup against Drew Anderson; while he is currently in the lineup, we are monitoring his status as he sits near our floor threshold. Finally, be advised of the 35% rain risk surrounding **Dylan Beavers**; although he didn't crack the primary lineup, the weather uncertainty further justifies keeping him on the bench while we prioritize the stability of our current starters.",
